Whether a number is even, with even and odd defined in terms of each other. The mutual form binds both names at once, so each function can call the other.
The probe is mutual recursion. It was the one probe the language could not express: with letrec alone, odd is not in scope where even is defined.
---
(lam n
  (mutual ((even (lam k (if (= k 0) 1 (odd (- k 1)))))
           (odd (lam k (if (= k 0) 0 (even (- k 1))))))
    (even n)))
---
0 => 1 fuel 10000
4 => 1 fuel 10000
7 => 0 fuel 10000
